209 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 153 0 R
/E (This report will give an accurate account of my internship experience at CTOS Basis, Petaling Jaya, Selangor as an Operations Assistance Intern for 24 weeks at the Menara CelcomDigi. The primary aim of this report is to demonstrate how I adjusted to the working environment of a real corporate structure, how I came to meet and work with a variety of people, and the development of my personal skills and financial knowledge in these 24 weeks. I was assigned to the Corporate Data Division and my job was to support and review business credit databases for companies in Malaysia and Singapore. I worked closely with the team that was based in Petaling Jaya and had to ensure that our financial data was accurate because it would get typed in by me and double checked by them; they had to check my company profiles and research legal cases to ensure the data in the database was completely correct.  )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 153 0 R
/E (In this report you will get my profile, the CTOS profile, a detailed training experience analysis, and a detailed SWOT analysis. I conducted a SWOT analysis to examine the strengths and weaknesses, opportunities and threats that is facing the company in the market so as to understand the position in which the company is in the market and give them some realistic tips on how they can improve. There are some positive aspects for CTOS, however, as it has more than 70% of the marketplace share and maintains a very huge database that maintains millions of consumers and businesses. The biggest problems they face, however, are their high technology infrastructure costs, and the fact that they still have a significant amount of manual data entry. In the future, CTOS has a lot of potential to expand its business in other ASEAN countries and move towards software subscription model. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 153 0 R
/E (Meanwhile, there are major competitive challenges posed by foreign competitors who are cutting prices and altering data privacy regulations that affect the ability to gather legal records. In general, this is my reflection on how I performed and how I see CTOS continuing to improve in the future.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
