/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
382 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (As an intern in the Corporate Data Division of CTOS Basis, Petaling Jaya, I became exposed to the back end functions of business-to-business \(B2B\) corporate intelligence. As an Operations Assistance Intern, working with my operations manager, Ms. Cheng Yen Ming, it was imperative that I have a complete focus on the data accuracy. I knew that my top priority was to ensure there were no data entry errors, or what I called a zero data entry error rate, because that's the information that the major banks and multi-national companies are using to make huge decisions.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
383 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 163 0 R
/T (3.2 Core Technical Tasks and Learning Experience )
/E (3.2 Core Technical Tasks and Learning Experience )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
384 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 163 0 R
/T (1. This course is designed for students wishing to learn how to enter and calculate financial data and ratios in advance.)
/E (1. This course is designed for students wishing to learn how to enter and calculate financial data and ratios in advance.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
385 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (My main tasks on the job were to review the companies' audited corporate financial reports  from Malaysia and Singapore. I was able to get raw data from the Profit & Loss \(P&L\) statement, the Balance Sheet, and the Cash Flow statements and enter them directly into the master system database.This wasn't just about inputting information; it was a hands-on opportunity to determine a company's financial well-being by working with financial ratios and calculations, including liquidity, debt to equity, and profitability ratios. It was very interesting to work with real-life corporate data and apply the financial theories I had acquired at University, and to understand how the operational decisions of a business can be reflected in the financial data.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
386 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 163 0 R
/T (2. Carrying out Bulk Orders for Corporate Clients.)
/E (2. Carrying out Bulk Orders for Corporate Clients.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
387 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (Ms. Cheng Yen Ming, our manager, tasked me with a very intensive part of my training work, which was to deal with bulk orders. I had to coordinate the processing of the pipeline of data when large institutional clients requested credit assessments or background screens for hundreds of vendor or vendor-prospect profiles at one time. By handling these bulk orders, I sharpened my time-management skills, and learned how to be extremely accurate even with a very heavy workload.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
