484 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 170 0 R
/E (CTOS should deploy advanced machine learning data-fusion tools to autonomously map executive connections across fragmented judicial networks. \(Scholars Digest Publishing, 2026\). CTOS Basis's extensive database of over 8 million commercial profiles, decades of court litigation history, and exclusive electronic Trade References \(eTR\) serve as the main corporate moat protecting it from new local competitors and straightforward data aggregators. )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
485 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 170 0 R
/E (However, legal filings, shareholder information, and winding-up petitions are dispersed among several judicial systems and register files, making raw commercial data frequently quite unstructured. These disparate data points can be automatically scanned, extracted, and joined by CTOS Basis using sophisticated machine learning-driven data-fusion techniques. Because of its computing capability, the platform can track corporate directorship networks on its own to find hidden operational risks. For example, it can identify whether a new business-to-business client is structurally connected to a sister firm that is currently involved in debt litigation. )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
