534 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 174 0 R
/E (The fluctuation in the global economy and geopolitical issues in key international markets, global institutional investors are turning to Malaysia as a preferred safe and stable investment base for debt products. This change sparked a huge increase in demand for Malaysian corporate bonds and fixed-income products. One of the big problems for foreign fund managers from financial hubs abroad, such as New York, London and Tokyo, is the difficulty of obtaining good, local data on credit risk and ESG scores \(Environmental, Social and Governance\) to assess these local bond issuers. Under local regulatory laws, )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
535 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 174 0 R
/E (CTOS Basis is not legally allowed to award official credit ratings directly, but under the control of the parent group, CTOS Basis holds 57.68% of the total shares in RAM Holdings Berhad, the top credit rating agency in Malaysia.  This strategic partnership presents an extremely attractive situation for CTOS Basis to circumvent the conventional regulatory hurdles. The companies can co-develop a complete Bond Risk and ESG Analytics Platform, which leverages CTOS's large-scale commercial data on more than 8 million business profiles and RAM's expertise in rating. )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [7]
>>
