569 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 177 0 R
/E (The CTOS Basis is a leading player in the corporate business intelligence market in Malaysia, but is being challenged by strong and formidable competitors like Experian Information Services Malaysia and Credit Bureau Malaysia \(CBM\) who are constantly pushing into the market. When it comes to business to business \(B2B\) sales, corporate buyers, such as large manufacturers, trade credit insurers, and multinational corporations are constantly seeking to improve their operating costs. Key accounts might move their business elsewhere if these large-scale competitors go on a price-crushing buying spree or if they offer a good discount if they buy in bulk for their corporations. A major drawback is that corporate credit verification information is derived from some shared public registries, such as the Companies Commission of Malaysia \(SSM\), which means that the competitors can simply package comparable financial information, resulting in possible price war.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
570 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 177 0 R
/E (In addition to price competition, the competition becomes even more potent when other players launch sophisticated, digital B2B solutions. The big boys, such as Global giants like Experian have deep financial pockets internationally and have the advanced machine learning capabilities that allows them to upgrade their commercial intelligence tools incredibly quickly. As competitors develop quicker international background checks, more efficient automated supply chain risk dashboards, or improved cross-border credit reporting frameworks based on regional partnerships, CTOS Basis' pace of change will begin to lag behind. If there are volume-based revenues from commercial transactions, then a loyal migration of major business clients or small and medium enterprise \(SME\) subscribers to a competitor's platform would come at a direct cost to the commercial division, in terms of market share loss and loss of steady volume-based transaction revenue.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
