>>
endobj
580 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 178 0 R
/E (The whole corporate structure of CTOS Basis is based on the collection, cross-referencing and sharing of rich commercial data, which is a highly sensitive business to the stringent regulatory framework such as Personal Data Protection Act \(PDPA\) in Malaysia. With the increasing scrutiny of data governance and consumer consent requirements by governments in Southeast Asia, the boundary between public corporate information and sensitive personal identity information \(PII\) like that of company directors, sole proprietors, and key shareholders is continuously shifting. They mean that CTOS Basis has to keep updating its software interfaces, redoing security protocols and even adding more legal and compliance staff every day. An aggressive tightening of the regulations could limit what data non-traditional data CTOS Basis can gather, delay delivery of reports and leave the company vulnerable to having significant amounts of data mishandled or face massive statutory fines or operational disruption if any data event occurs.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
